      <Graphics lineColor="000000" lineStyle="Solid" lineWidth="1.0" connectorType="Straight" />
      <Comment source="BioCyc">Heme proteins with histidine as proximal ligand. The iron in the resting enzyme is Fe(III). They also peroxidize non-phenolic substrates such as |FRAME: CPD-12812 3,3&apos;,5,5&apos;-tetramethylbenzidine| (TMB) and |FRAME: CPD-12796 2,2&apos;-azino-bis-(3-ethylbenzothiazoline-6-sulfonate)| (ABTS). Certain peroxidases (e.g. lactoperoxidase, SBP) oxidize bromide, iodide and thiocyanate.</Comment>
